{"id":"NCT07449702","title":"An Open-Label Extension Study of ORKA-001 in Participants With Plaque Psoriasis","official":"An Open-label Extension Study to Evaluate the Long-term Safety, Tolerability, and Efficacy of ORKA-001 in Participants With Moderate-to-Severe Plaque Psoriasis","summary":"An open-label extension (OLE) study to evaluate the long-term safety and efficacy of ORKA-001 in adult participants with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis, who previously participated in an Oruka Therapeutics sponsored study.","conditions":["Plaque Psoriasis"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"ORKA-001"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n1. Signed informed consent by participants from previous trial choosing to transition into the OLE.\n2. Participants who have successfully completed the preceding trial.\n3. For women of childbearing potential, must have a negative urine pregnancy test at Baseline visit.\n4. For women of childbearing potential and fertile male participants with a partner of childbearing potential must be willing to continue to use highly effective contraception\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n1. Participants who experienced any adverse events with ORKA-001 in the preceding trial that led to permanent investigational medicinal product discontinuation or, in the opinion of the Investigator, would preclude continued treatment with ORKA-001\n2. Participants who have developed guttate, erythrodermic or pustular psoriasis or drug-induced psoriasis (as diagnosed by the Investigator), during the preceding trial.\n3. Evidence of current or previous clinically significant disease, medical condition other than psoriasis, or finding during the medical examination that, in the opinion of the Investigator would compromise the safety of the participant or the quality of the data.\n4. Any clinically significant laboratory abnormality based on the last available lab results received during the preceding trial, that, according to the Investigator's medical assessment, precludes them from continued treatment with ORKA-001.\n5. Participant is pregnant or breastfeeding.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":240,"start":"2026-02-23","pcd":"2030-05","upd":"2026-10-23","sponsor":"Oruka Therapeutics, Inc.","areas":["other"],"central":["Oruka Clinical Trials Information · 781-560-0299 · clinicaltrials@orukatx.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Oruka Therapeutics Investigative Site","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85032","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":"Oruka Therapeutics Investigative Site · 781-560-0299 · clinicaltrials@orukatx.com"},{"f":"Oruka Therapeutics Investigative Site","city":"North Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72117","s":"R","lat":34.7695,"lon":-92.2671,"c":"Oruka Investigative Site · 781-560-0299 · clinicaltrials@orukatx.com"},{"f":"Oruka Therapeutics Investigative Site","city":"Fountain Valley","pr":"California","zip":"92708","s":"R","lat":33.7092,"lon":-117.9537,"c":"Oruka Investigative Site · 781-560-0299 · clinicaltrials@orukatx.com"},{"f":"Oruka Therapeutics Investigative Site","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90045","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Oruka Investigative Site · 781-560-0299 · clinicaltrials@orukatx.com"},{"f":"Oruka Therapeutics Investigative Site","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90095","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Oruka Investigative Site · 781-560-0299 · clinicaltrials@orukatx.com"},{"f":"Oruka Therapeutics Investigative Site","city":"San Diego","pr":"California","zip":"92123","s":"R","lat":32.7157,"lon":-117.1647,"c":"Oruka Investigative Site · 781-560-0299 · clinicaltrials@orukatx.com"},{"f":"Oruka Therapeutics Investigative Site","city":"Santa Ana","pr":"California","zip":"92701","s":"R","lat":33.7456,"lon":-117.8678,"c":"Oruka Investigative Site · 781-560-0299 · clinicaltrials@orukatx.com"},{"f":"Oruka Therapeutics Investigative Site","city":"Santa Monica","pr":